      "message": "test(app): read a reset or EOF as the idle drop in the trickling-client test\n\nThe server closes a trickling client with its bytes still unread, so the\nclose may reset the connection and discard the idle note. The test read\nthat reset as \"never dropped\". A reset, abort, broken pipe or EOF now is\nthe drop; a read that times out (client still connected) still fails, and\nthe window timing asserts are unchanged. No retries, no longer sleeps.\n\nFixes #1366\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
